Take the real <filesystem> on this console, and do not mistake clang for GCC 8

`filesystem.h` uses the standard header when the compiler has one and falls back to the bundled
`ghc::filesystem` otherwise. Two arms of its condition exclude this build, and only one of them
was meant to.

**`!__FreeBSD__`** carries a comment recording that FreeBSD's implementation "appears problematic
(on version 13.0-BETA1 with clang 11)". That is an observation about one system libc++ in 2021.
This target is FreeBSD-derived but its C++ library is a freestanding libc++ built from source in
this tree, five years newer, whose `<filesystem>` is built and works here. Lifted for this
platform only - `__PROSPERO__` - so a real FreeBSD build keeps upstream's behaviour exactly.

**`!(defined(__GNUC__) && __GNUC__ < 9)` excludes clang, which is not what it says.** Clang
defines `__GNUC__` as **4** - it has masqueraded as GCC 4.2.1 for its whole life - so this arm
rejects every clang, at every version, on every platform. The comment above it says "GCC 8: its
implementation requires linking an extra library", which is about libstdc++ and has nothing to do
with clang or libc++. Adding `!defined(__clang__)` makes the test mean what the comment says.

That second one is not specific to this console: any clang build of Pomme silently takes ghc
today, including on Linux with a perfectly good `<filesystem>`.

Taking the standard header rather than ghc is not a preference. ghc wants a full POSIX filesystem
underneath it - `st_dev`/`st_ino` file identity, hard links, `utimensat`, the `*at()` family,
`std::wstring` - and this console has almost none of that, so each would have been a stub propping
up a library whose model does not fit. libc++'s own implementation wanted eleven declarations, all
of which had an honest answer, and `realpath` among them is complete rather than refused: the only
thing it does that this filesystem cannot is resolve symbolic links, and there are none.
---
diff --git a/extern/Pomme/src/CompilerSupport/filesystem.h b/extern/Pomme/src/CompilerSupport/filesystem.h
index 1bcff28..1a24692 100644
--- a/extern/Pomme/src/CompilerSupport/filesystem.h
+++ b/extern/Pomme/src/CompilerSupport/filesystem.h
@@ -6,8 +6,8 @@
 // - GCC 8: its implementation requires linking an extra library; don't bother with that
 
 #if !__APPLE__ \
-	&& !__FreeBSD__ \
-	&& !(defined(__GNUC__) && __GNUC__ < 9) \
+	&& !(defined(__FreeBSD__) && !defined(__PROSPERO__)) \
+	&& !(defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__clang__) && __GNUC__ < 9) \
 	&& defined(__cplusplus) && __cplusplus >= 201703L \
 	&& defined(__has_include) && __has_include(<filesystem>)
 
